                <pb facs="0025" n="11" sameAs="frus:frus1943v06/pg11"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/32339: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-12-16T20:00:00-04:00">December 16, 1943—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1548. You may inform Foreign Minister, with reference to your 2302, December 15,
                    4 p.m., that this Government considers the declaration <pb facs="0026" n="12"
                        xml:id="pg12"/> by United Nations a “Declaration”, as stated in the title of
                    the document; that consequently it has not been submitted to the Senate as a
                    treaty.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
